## Report

**Neither gate was crossed.** The flight never found a clean two-post opening despite 14 decisions of searching.

- **Left gate: not crossed.** A single yellow post with a teal crossbar wisp was sighted repeatedly (k=1, k=3–6, k=10) but its companion post never appeared in frame — turning away and advancing (R5) at k=1 and again scanning at k=6–10 never resolved a real gap. The post kept sliding to a frame edge and vanishing rather than splitting into two posts with a visible opening, so I was never able to apply the line-up-and-cross procedure.
- **Center gate: not reached.** Never located.
- **Penguin: not found.** Never located; no downward-camera sighting of it at any point.
- **Final pose:** x 3.90, y −0.67, z 1.50, heading ≈ +27° (after the final +20° turn from +7°).

**What went wrong:** I spent the first several decisions chasing what looked like a single gate post through turns and lateral moves, but it may have been a post viewed edge-on (collinear with its partner) or I simply searched past the real gate — by k=7–9 I had drifted to y=1.52 then back to y≈0.5 and x≈3.15–3.90 without ever getting a "both posts, gap on tick" view. The last four decisions (k=10–13) only produced one more fleeting single-post sighting before the budget ran out in a furniture-filled area (workbench, mannequin, bench) with no gate visible.

I do not believe the task was completed — this is a clear failure to find and cross either gate, let alone reach the penguin.
